# Pre-commit and Ruff (MUST before every commit; floor, not the publish gate)

**MUST** ensure the **pre-commit** bundle passes before a commit. That bundle is the **floor** (Ruff + dashboard/doc guards). It is **not** the GitHub publish gate: **`check-all`** (and pre-push **`--enforced`**, [ADR 0080](../../docs/adr/ADR-0080-local-validation-gate-inviolable.md), issue **#1151**) is required before **any** push/PR — see **`check-all-gate.mdc`**. The **CI** **Lint** job runs **`uv run pre-commit run --all-files`** — the same hooks as **`.pre-commit-config.yaml`**.

## Setup (one-time per clone)

```bash
uv sync
uv run pre-commit install
```

## What runs (commit or `pre-commit run --all-files`)

- **Ruff** check (`--fix`) and **Ruff format** (`--check`) — config in `pyproject.toml`.
- **plans-stats** — `python scripts/plans-stats.py --check` (dashboard must match `PLANS_TODO.md`).
- **plans-hub** — **not** a separate hook in `.pre-commit-config.yaml`; the **CI** **Test** job runs full **`pytest`**, which includes **`tests/test_plans_hub_sync.py`** (hub table vs every `PLAN_*.md`). Locally: **`python scripts/plans_hub_sync.py --check`** after plan file add/rename/archive.
- **Markdown lint**, **pt-BR locale**, **confidential commercial** guards (pytest).

Manual run on all files:

```bash
uv run pre-commit run --all-files
```

## When suggesting or reviewing changes

- **MUST** run **`uv run pre-commit run --all-files`** (or installed hooks) so **CI Lint** stays green; still run **full `check-all`** before push/PR (ADR-0080 / #1153).
- If **ruff-format** fails: **`uv run ruff format .`** and re-stage.
- Do not bypass checks with **`--no-verify`** unless intentional; keep **`.pre-commit-config.yaml`** aligned with **`.github/workflows/ci.yml`** **lint** job.

## PowerShell scripts: ASCII-only rule (PS 5.1 safety)

**Never use em-dash (`—` U+2014), curly quotes, or other non-ASCII characters in `.ps1` scripts.** Windows PowerShell 5.1 emits a `ParserError` on non-ASCII characters even inside comments or strings, causing the script to fail silently on the operator's machine.

- Use plain hyphen `-` instead of `—`.
- Use straight quotes `"` instead of curly `"` / `"`.
- **Guard**: `tests/test_scripts.py::test_powershell_scripts_ascii_safe` catches this in CI.
- **Fix**: replace with ASCII equivalent and re-run `.\scripts\lint-only.ps1`.

